2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2408) 'dev.1: one person visits the station
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2408) '- The pen's `v20261001-dev.1` tag marks dev.1, and the prerelease carries the double engine `v20260930-double.1`, the addon `v20260930-addon.1` and the five guest ELFs, each against `SHA256SUMS`.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2408) '- The four ported modules (`environment`, `station`, `plaza`, `sakura`), each a faithful port of the pinned original, send their 1089 primitive colliders and the terrain height field to the MuJoCo guest as the original's `physics.js` calls make them.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2408) '- RFD66606-2293, where this rule lived before the split.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2408) '- RFD66606-2262, the release ladder this rung follows.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2408) 'The station port is abandoned
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2408) 'RFD66606-2384, the module-by-module port, is abandoned (operator, 2026-11-11). The plaza's assets and tech stay in use, and baking goes through slughorn.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2408) 'The walker and world grab
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2408) 'A walker ported from the original's `player.js` (radius 0.3 m, height 1.7 m, step 0.45 m) runs on the guest's ray and contact queries, read through rx's stick movement and rotation components, with a 30 degree snap turn and teleport; there is no jump. World grab is off by default and sits in a three-wedge radial (hold B or Y, tilt, release: world grab, recentre, exit).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2408) 'Gates
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2408) 'Gates: `gate_colliders` in &{repo("entities-sakuragaoka-station")} (every collider matches the original's, with `drop_one` and `shift` as controls), run by hand because that repository has no CI. And `gate_locomotion` in the pen's `double.yml` (walk, step-up and the refused 1.25 m ledge, the handrail stopping the walker, snap turn, teleport landing and refused, and bit-identical poses across two runs), with the controls `step_high`, `no_resolve`, `solid_land` and `ulp`, each of which must fail.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2408) 'Playable, and the gap
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2408) 'Playable, as the persona run on 2026-10-02 showed: walk from the plaza toward the station, snap turn, teleport, reach the forecourt, and toggle world grab from the radial. The persona did not reach the platform or climb the stairs. The locomotion gate climbs the six treads headless. Past the four modules the terrain is open where the town's houses and shops stand in the original. The logbook names that gap and counts five others.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2408  1 LINE
 Text:Written

